146
00:11:41,120 --> 00:11:45,400
The branch table will show one if a branch at that address alias was taken last time

147
00:11:45,400 --> 00:11:53,400
and zero if it was not.

148
00:11:53,400 --> 00:11:55,360
Let's see how this works with an example.

149
00:11:55,360 --> 00:12:00,080
Here, we're predicting the branch equal instruction upon each iteration of the loop.

150
00:12:00,080 --> 00:12:04,640
In the first iteration, we read the prediction from the BHT.

151
00:12:04,640 --> 00:12:07,680
In this case, let's say the BHT entry is zero.

152
00:12:07,680 --> 00:12:11,840
So we predict that we will not take the branch.

153
00:12:11,840 --> 00:12:15,880
Then let's say it turns out that the branch is actually taken.

154
00:12:15,880 --> 00:12:22,360
So we need to update the prediction accordingly to predict taken next time.

155
00:12:22,360 --> 00:12:26,800
This algorithm continues where on each iteration, our prediction is the last outcome of the

156
00:12:26,800 --> 00:12:29,160
